# ShellCheck settings for the shellspec suites only.
#
# Checked against upstream before adding anything here: shellspec's own repo
# ships a root `.shellcheckrc` containing exactly `disable=SC2317`, and its docs
# say only that spec syntax "is compatible with shell scripts, and you can embed
# shell functions and use ShellCheck to check the syntax". There is no published
# strategy for the DSL itself.
#
# SC2317 (unreachable command) matches upstream. ShellCheck parses `Describe` /
# `It` / `Mock` / `End` as ordinary commands, decides nothing can run past a
# `Mock ... End` block, and reports every later example as dead code.
#
# SC2329 (function never invoked) goes beyond upstream, and each finding was
# checked rather than assumed: all three are spec-local helpers invoked through
# `When call`, which ShellCheck cannot see through. The check postdates
# shellspec's config, which is likely why upstream has not hit it.
#
# Scoped to spec/ rather than the repo root, which is stricter than upstream:
# both checks are worth keeping against the plugin scripts, which are real
# shell. Do not promote this file to the root.
disable=SC2317,SC2329
